From lucas at debian.org  Sun Mar  1 20:51:26 2026
From: lucas at debian.org (Lucas Nussbaum)
Date: Sun, 1 Mar 2026 21:51:26 +0100
Subject: [R-pkg-team] Bug#1129454: r-cran-terra: debaudit/git2dsc regression
 in 1.8-93-1: 330 - failed to guess tag
Message-ID: <aaSmzte5LfYgF7LP@grub.nussbaum.fr>

Source: r-cran-terra
Version: 1.8-93-1
Severity: minor
User: lucas at debian.org
Usertags: debaudit

Hi,

While working on https://debaudit.debian.net/, I ran into an issue with
r-cran-terra/1.8-93-1, which is currently in unstable and trying to migrate to
forky.

debaudit detects the following issue in unstable:
> 330 - failed to guess tag
Debaudit could not identify a Git tag in the repository specified by
Vcs-Git for this version. Maybe the tag was not pushed?

You can find more details at:
https://debaudit.debian.net/git2dsc/result/520710b04887540cf06905ab10275ca831c726b507cec4a588e4c0b4e54d727f

The version in forky (1.8-70-1) tested fine, with the following diagnostic:
> 910 - git-generated dsc identical to archive dsc after normalization
You can find its result at: https://debaudit.debian.net/git2dsc/result/cd36832868b283bbc3702ecd5654366450c31af06c493cedd47d5eed4514ce3f

Since Debaudit is in heavy development, I am very interested in hearing if the
issue was misdetected somehow.

Thanks,

Lucas Nussbaum


